# 14. RUBRIC EVALUATOR

Implement a working rubric-based evaluation system for Faculty.

A Rubric Evaluator assesses a project or assignment against configurable criteria and provides a consistent score and feedback.

Example criteria:

| Criterion | Example weight |
|---|---:|
| Problem understanding | 15% |
| Functionality and implementation | 25% |
| Code quality and design | 15% |
| Innovation and creativity | 15% |
| Testing and validation | 15% |
| Documentation and presentation | 15% |
| Total | 100% |

These are examples only. Authorized Faculty must be able to configure the criteria and weights.

## Evaluation workflow

1. Faculty selects an assigned project or assessment.
2. Faculty selects a rubric.
3. The application displays criteria and weights.
4. Faculty enters scores and comments.
5. The application calculates the weighted result.
6. Faculty reviews the result.
7. Faculty saves the evaluation.
8. Scores and comments persist in the database.
9. Faculty can reopen saved evaluations.
10. Students see feedback only when it is published or otherwise permitted.

For scores out of 10:

`Criterion contribution = (Score / 10) × Criterion weight`

Sum all contributions to calculate a score out of 100 when weights total 100%.

Validate the score ranges and weight totals.

Optional AI evaluation must be labelled as a suggestion. Faculty must approve the final grade. AI must not invent evidence or claim it executed code that it did not run.

Do not leave a nonfunctional Rubric Evaluator tab.

